	(text "Programming connector (ICSP): MCLR, PGC1, PGD1 (shared with PA6H_RX), GND.\nNo VDD pin: the board must be powered while flashing.\nMCLR: R4 10k pull-up + C6 100nF (PIC24F16KA102 datasheet, §2.3).\nThe 100-470 Ω series resistor of the reference circuit is not fitted."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 185.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0c07db5c-733b-4f39-946b-d6c316a5b006")
	)
	(text "MS5611 in I2C mode (PS tied to PROUT), R1 / R2 10k I2C pull-ups.\nCSB (pin 4) tied to GND -> I2C address 0x77. Pin 5 is a second CSB pad, connected internally: left unconnected.\nSDO is unused in I2C mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.646 80.518 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "16fdcde0-c761-44d2-bb26-60642f3531d0")
	)
	(text "Button: pulls SWITCH to GND, R6 10k pull-up to PROUT, read on PIC RB15."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 243.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "302fdfb5-39d4-41bc-bf4c-f6f962700f16")
	)
	(text "MAS6240 piezo driver: DIN = AUDIO_OUT (PIC OC1), EN1 / EN2 from PIC RA2 / RA3.\nC5 / C7: charge-pump capacitors (CN1-CP1, CN2-CP2), C8 on VOUT.\nBuzzer between VO1 (through R7) and VO2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "34eee771-9c52-4aab-a81d-d573ed8933e1")
	)
	(text "GPS NMEA (PA6H_TX) reaches the Kobo RX (KOBO_RX) through R5 (1k).\nThe PIC U1TX drives KOBO_RX directly and sends the vario data between GPS bursts.\nPA6H_TX also goes to PIC INT1 (RB14) to detect the start of each burst.\nPA6H VCC comes from KOBO_EN, V_BACKUP from BATT+."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 107.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "65a2c786-53a8-4edc-aaa8-9fc714ac98d9")
	)
	(text "Power supply sheet: BATT+ (Kobo battery) -> ADP160 LDO -> PROUT.\nKOBO_EN (Kobo connector) enables the LDO and also supplies the PA6H GPS VCC directly."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 226.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "b5661e0e-a34f-4039-a366-f16e75dd5b6f")
	)
